Translation patch: RISTRETTO_BASEPOINT_TABLE (src/constants.rs)

Change: The pointer cast
`&*(ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE as *const EdwardsBasepointTable as *const RistrettoBasepointTable)`
(in an `unsafe` block) becomes
`&RistrettoBasepointTable(EdwardsBasepointTable(ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE.0))`: the static is
built by copying the table's array of lookup tables into a new `RistrettoBasepointTable`
instead of reinterpreting the pointer to the Ed25519 table.

Why: Charon turns the cast into a raw borrow (`&raw const`), which Aeneas rejects
("Unsupported operation"), so the original could only be translated as opaque.

Behaviour: **same value, different memory.** `RistrettoBasepointTable` is a `#[repr(transparent)]`
wrapper of `EdwardsBasepointTable` and the copy rebuilds the whole value from its only field,
so every multiplication through it reads the same entries and returns the same result. The
initializer is evaluated at compile time (no new runtime work or panic). The difference: the
binary holds a second copy of the table data (32 x 8 x 3 field elements x 40 B = 30,720 B) and
`RISTRETTO_BASEPOINT_TABLE` no longer has the same address as `*ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE`.
Nothing in the crate compares these addresses; the static is `pub`, so downstream code
could.
(Context is plain rather than `-W`: a `static` has no function boundary, so `-W` would
include the whole file above it.)

Facts relied on (not visible in the diff): `EdwardsBasepointTable` is `pub struct EdwardsBasepointTable(pub(crate) [LookupTableRadix16<AffineNielsPoint>; 32])`
(src/edwards.rs, generated by `impl_basepoint_table!`): `.0` is its only field and is `Copy`
(the lookup tables and `AffineNielsPoint` derive `Copy`), hence has no interior mutability.
`ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE: &'static EdwardsBasepointTable`. Reading a static from a static
initializer needs Rust >= 1.83; the crate's MSRV is 1.85. The only in-crate use is
`scalar * constants::RISTRETTO_BASEPOINT_TABLE` in `RistrettoPoint::mul_base`.

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file, add the static back to `opaque` in Cargo.toml if needed,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh and `lake build`, and check both succeed.

